      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, line 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Officers, executive board members and board of governors members are volunteers. There is no compensation for these individuals. The managers (operations and merchandising), sales associates and bookkeeper for the gift corner are compensated. These salaries are approved by the executive board salaries committee and are determined based on past wages and hours expected to be worked. The gift corner provides the funds for overall activities of the KOSC and the wages paid to employees are minimal but comparative to other such operations on other bases in Okinawa.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, line 18</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Every executive board member should have a copy of the governing documents and the conflict of interest policy in their continuity binders. Anyone wishing to see these documents may contact any member of the executive board to review these documents and financial statements. Annual financial statements are maintained at the Kadena Gift Corner located in building # 436 on Kadena AFB. Monthly financial statements are prepared for the gift corner, general fund and charitable fund by their respective treasurers. Each preparer maintains a copy of their respective reports in their continuity binder. The monthly financial statements are submitted to the executive board prior to its montly meetings. The monthly board reports are documented and are in the monthly minutes recorded by the recording secretary. Anyone wishing to view these should contact an executive board member who can then arrange to get a copy of the requested documents.</ExplanationTxt>
